 "notes": "Dark-matter axion-photon haloscope (laser-interferometric polarisation-rotation detector). Curve traced from Fig. 2, the black 'LIDA (95% C.L.)' curve (vector path in ancillary sensitivity.pdf, path index 300, 386 points downsampled to 42). Calibration: y-axis log g_agamma via decade gridlines (10^-11 at y=499.0, 10^-8 at y=317.7); x-axis axion mass in neV via bottom-axis labels (1.97 neV at x=168.0, 2.04 neV at x=452.5), converted to eV. Extracted minimum (best sensitivity) 1.51e-10 GeV^-1 at 1.986 neV, matching the paper's stated peak 1.51e-10 GeV^-1 at 1.985 neV. The paper's headline measurement band is 1.97-2.01 neV (average sensitivity 3.2e-10 GeV^-1); the plotted 95% C.L. curve extends slightly beyond (1.9666-2.0452 neV) and is reported as plotted. g_agamma defined via L = -(g_agamma/4) a F Ftilde, already the canonical convention. Density: the limit scales with rho_DM but the paper quotes no numerical local density value, so dm_density_assumed is null. Curve is intrinsically spiky (per-mass 95% C.L. sensitivity).",
